codex
A safer setup-based variant is now the main candidate: precompute the antithetic whitened Gaussian probes once from `context.seed`, then spend the per-MLP FLOPs on forward passes instead of rebuilding the same kind of probe cloud each time. I’m testing whether the changed probe stream hurts or helps on synthetic default-shape MLPs.
