The high-sample check showed the fixed setup probe can be much worse, so I’m not going to ship it as-is. I’m checking a variant that keeps setup precomputation but applies a cheap `mlp.seed`-derived coordinate sign flip, which restores per-MLP randomness without rebuilding the whole whitened cloud.
